1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,205
Imagine losing money

2
00:00:01,205 --> 00:00:01,685
to a trader

3
00:00:01,685 --> 00:00:02,836
you can't even see.

4
00:00:03,742 --> 00:00:04,655
Because in India's

5
00:00:04,655 --> 00:00:05,407
OPTIONS MARKET

6
00:00:05,407 --> 00:00:06,665
you're not just competing

7
00:00:06,665 --> 00:00:08,346
with other humans anymore.

8
00:00:09,113 --> 00:00:10,220
You're competing with

9
00:00:10,220 --> 00:00:10,610
ALGORITHMS

10
00:00:10,610 --> 00:00:12,020
that can execute trades

11
00:00:12,020 --> 00:00:13,619
in fractions of a second.

12
00:00:14,519 --> 00:00:15,425
And the numbers

13
00:00:15,425 --> 00:00:16,210
are crazy.

14
00:00:17,085 --> 00:00:19,125
According to a SEBI study

15
00:00:19,125 --> 00:00:20,515
reported by Bloomberg,

16
00:00:20,515 --> 00:00:21,955
Indian retail traders lost

17
00:00:21,955 --> 00:00:24,128
around $33 BILLION

18
00:00:24,128 --> 00:00:25,780
in equity derivatives

19
00:00:25,780 --> 00:00:26,905
over four years

20
00:00:26,905 --> 00:00:28,991
through March 2025.

21
00:00:29,977 --> 00:00:31,500
At the same time,

22
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:33,510
algorithm-driven trading companies

23
00:00:33,510 --> 00:00:35,865
made around $7 BILLION

24
00:00:35,865 --> 00:00:36,775
in gross profit

25
00:00:36,775 --> 00:00:38,442
from India's options market

26
00:00:38,442 --> 00:00:40,521
in just one financial year.

27
00:00:41,569 --> 00:00:42,585
So how do these firms

28
00:00:42,585 --> 00:00:44,117
get such an advantage?

29
00:00:45,058 --> 00:00:45,905
SPEED

30
00:00:46,534 --> 00:00:48,320
Their computers can analyse

31
00:00:48,320 --> 00:00:50,485
market data and execute trades

32
00:00:50,485 --> 00:00:51,530
in MICROSECONDS

33
00:00:51,530 --> 00:00:52,815
or even faster —

34
00:00:52,815 --> 00:00:54,430
while you're still looking

35
00:00:54,430 --> 00:00:56,340
at the chart on your phone.

36
00:00:57,090 --> 00:00:59,005
And these firms spend millions

37
00:00:59,005 --> 00:01:00,750
on technology, servers

38
00:01:00,750 --> 00:01:02,456
and ultra-fast connections

39
00:01:02,456 --> 00:01:03,875
just to gain tiny

40
00:01:03,875 --> 00:01:05,289
speed advantages.

41
00:01:06,044 --> 00:01:06,780
But here's the

42
00:01:06,780 --> 00:01:07,672
important part…

43
00:01:08,829 --> 00:01:10,430
This doesn't automatically mean

44
00:01:10,430 --> 00:01:12,030
algorithms are stealing money

45
00:01:12,030 --> 00:01:13,269
from retail traders.

46
00:01:14,210 --> 00:01:15,990
High-frequency trading can also

47
00:01:15,990 --> 00:01:17,399
improve liquidity

48
00:01:17,399 --> 00:01:19,542
and make markets more efficient.

49
00:01:20,900 --> 00:01:23,165
The bigger issue is the massive

50
00:01:23,165 --> 00:01:24,180
TECHNOLOGY GAP

51
00:01:24,180 --> 00:01:25,652
between a retail trader

52
00:01:25,652 --> 00:01:27,926
and a professional trading firm.

53
00:01:29,303 --> 00:01:30,450
So next time you see

54
00:01:30,450 --> 00:01:32,002
a stock move suddenly…

55
00:01:33,402 --> 00:01:34,085
Remember:

56
00:01:34,648 --> 00:01:36,010
There might be a machine

57
00:01:36,010 --> 00:01:37,055
trading against you

58
00:01:37,055 --> 00:01:38,335
before you even realise

59
00:01:38,335 --> 00:01:39,197
what's happening.
